    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2026-07-15 21:25:00 MDT Expires: 2026-07-15 22:15:00 MDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways. Target Area: Eastern Box Elder County At 925 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10 miles north of Howell, or 16 miles northwest of Tremonton, moving east at 10 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible.\nThis storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northern Box Elder County.",
